This term not only means to go, to depart, but also to be liberated, to go forth in freedom.

c0008
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:21.000
It is the same term usually translated as Exodus describing Israel's departure from the house of bondage in Egypt.

c0009
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:42.012
Within the context of our story it means that Abraham and Sarah when well advanced in years he was 75 and she was 65 years old broke away from the system of values enslaving them and started a new life

c0010
00:02:42.012 --> 00:02:49.012
A life that rejuvenated them both spiritually and biologically.

c0011
00:02:49.012 --> 00:03:12.012
Abraham lived 100 years more. And Sarah 62. Indeed, about a thousand years later, when the people of Israel were in material and spiritual decline, Isaiah calls forth the figures of Abraham and Sarah to inspire them to overcome their despair.

c0012
