And I blessed him, that is spiritually, and increased him, that is materially.

c0015
00:03:39.012 --> 00:03:47.052
In order to grasp Abraham's spiritual bondage, it will be necessary to consider some of the

c0016
00:03:47.052 --> 00:03:53.292
essential features of Mesopotamian civilization.

c0017
00:03:53.292 --> 00:04:03.612
Since early antiquity, there were two dominant civilizations flourishing, one in Egypt and

c0018
00:04:03.612 --> 00:04:13.212
And the other in Mesopotamia, with totally different philosophies of men and society.

c0019
00:04:13.212 --> 00:04:23.872
Mesopotamia rejected the idea of one single omnipotent God. Individually, the gods of

c0020
00:04:23.872 --> 00:04:34.592
The Babylonian pantheon held only limited power. Ultimate power resided in the totality

c0021
00:04:34.592 --> 00:04:41.152
of the gods. It was the effect of different configurations and alliances established by

c0022
00:04:41.152 --> 00:04:53.632
the gods and therefore subject to manipulation. These alliances were revised every year, giving

c0023
00:04:53.632 --> 00:05:06.204
Rays to new configurations of power and ideologies This concept of religion was a replica of the political system

c0024
00:05:06.204 --> 00:05:12.344
The Mesopotamian king did not represent absolute power.

c0025
00:05:12.344 --> 00:05:19.504
The authority of the king was limited by the power of the gods above and the consensus

c0026
00:05:19.504 --> 00:05:48.504
The elders below to whom he was accountable. They also conceived of a cosmic and impersonal law called Kitum, to which even the king was its humble servant. In this way, the rights of the individual were protected and the abuses of authority checked.

c0027
00:05:49.504 --> 00:06:01.504
In many significant aspects, the Mesopotamian society resembled our own modern society in the West.

c0028
00:06:01.504 --> 00:06:10.504
Scholars have pointed out our debt to Mesopotamian civilization, particularly in the fields of government.

c0029
00:06:10.504 --> 00:06:17.504
Democracy seems to have been a Mesopotamian invention. Law and science.

c0030
00:06:17.504 --> 00:06:42.504
Perhaps this is why it is so easy for us to understand the frustration of a 75 years old man at the twilight of his life with the melodies of a society that produces spiritual anarchy, intellectual relativism, social apathy and bewilderment.

c0031
00:06:42.504 --> 00:07:04.504
A distinguished ancient Near Eastern scholar observed, the collapse of Nineveh and Babylon was due not so much to the superiority of outside powers as to the crushing weight of the internal structure.

c0032
00:07:04.504 --> 00:07:17.364
The Tower of Bavel is the symbol of a society without absolutes. It represents the society

c0033
00:07:17.364 --> 00:07:37.036
in which genuine human communication is excluded The individual is condemned to existential The solitude deafened by the tumult of languages he cannot possibly understand

c0034
00:07:58.876 --> 00:08:02.876
society and goes searching for the promised land.

c0035
00:08:05.916 --> 00:08:17.196
In his journey away from Mesopotamia, Abraham is stretching his hand to everyone who can feel the

c0036
00:08:17.196 --> 00:08:23.356
anguish of an individual without ultimate goals and aspirations.

c0037
00:08:25.036 --> 00:08:32.036
Let us hold his hand and follow his footsteps into the Promised Land.

c0038
00:08:37.516 --> 00:08:44.516
At the time of the Patriarchs, the land of Canaan was a scarcely populated area inhabited

c0039
00:08:44.796 --> 00:08:51.796
by people of Semitic and non-Semitic background. Both economically and culturally, it was a

