personal authority of the Pharaoh. The people of Egypt, regardless of their social status

c0047
00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:52.680
The

c0048
00:10:52.680 --> 00:11:04.640
In the annals of history, as slaves of Pharaoh, the individuals had no rights, but they enjoyed

c0049
00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:17.020
absolute stability. In Egypt, time was static. There was no real past or future. Changes

c0050
00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:26.520
These were superficial disturbances of the established order. The present was overwhelming

c0051
00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:38.780
and irremovable. In a profound sense, ancient Egypt is an excellent illustration of totalitarianism

c0052
00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:42.780
